Copy image regions by rows and alpha runs.

An opaque region was copied one pixel at a time; copy each row at once.
Sources with alpha are mostly runs of opaque and transparent pixels: find
them four alpha values at a time, copy the opaque ones by rows and skip the
transparent ones. Blend the rest with red and blue weighed together in
place, which gives the same pixels as the per-channel arithmetic.

